<title>NORWAY: Statkraft signs NOK 3.5 bln Indonesian deal.</title>
<headline>Statkraft signs NOK 3.5 bln Indonesian deal.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norway's state power generator Statkraft AS said on Thursday it had signed a letter of intent with Indonesian state power company PT PLN (Persero) on the joint development of Merangin 2, a hydroelectric power station in Jambi proviNce in Sumatra.  </p>
<p>Total costs for the plant were estimated at 3.5 billion crowns, according to a Statkraft statement to the Oslo bourse.</p>
<p>The project includes tunnels and a mountain power station with a capacity to produce 1.5 terawatt hours per year.</p>
<p>Commercial operations were expected to begin in 2003.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
